### 8. Report

When the loop halts (any reason — per the 6 safety rails above):

```
loop done — converged=<bool> iter=<N>/<max_iter>  mode=<mode>
  objective: <objective>
  target: <target or "(all features)">
  completed: <count>/<total>  [<names...>]
  stop_reason: <reason>
  spec: <spec path>
  context: work-docs/loop-context/<slug>.yaml
```

**Prefix is part of the schema.** The first token MUST be `loop done`.
The variants `loop paused`, `loop stopped`, `loop suspended`, `loop hold`
are NOT in the schema — they are anti-pattern outputs flagged by the
self-pause prohibition rail (Section 4 "Safety rails"). If you find
yourself about to emit such a prefix, the correct path is to either
run `/compact` (context pressure) or halt via safety rail #3 with
`stop_reason="blocked: ..."` (genuine blocker).

**`stop_reason` is constrained.** It must be one of:
- `max_iter (<N>) reached`
- `time_cap (<N>h) reached`
- `<N> consecutive failures`
- `feature <name> retried <N> times`
- `Gate 0 exhausted retries on <stage>`
- `stopping criteria met` (improve mode convergence)
- `blocked: <one-sentence reason>` (escape hatch via failed_streak)
- `user interrupt` (explicit operator Ctrl+C / /esc from outside the loop body)

Any other `stop_reason` string is a regression — surface it as a bug
report, do not normalize it into the schema.

For non-converged halts, also emit:
- In-flight feature/cycle when stopped
- Last failure reason (if `failed_streak > 0`)
- One concrete suggestion (raise `--max-iter`, narrow stopping_criteria,
  split a failing feature, etc.)

For `improve` mode convergence, emit a brief quality summary:
- Issues found in final review (by severity count)
- Test result from last cycle
- Which stopping_criteria items are satisfied

