## P5 batch mode — `/hm:loop p5-batch-N` (PLAN-total-spec-coverage ADR-013 R2)

When `<goal>` begins with `p5-batch` (e.g. `/hm:loop p5-batch-1`,
`/hm:loop p5-batch-all`), this is the prompt-driven SPEC bulk-authoring path.
It is **extracted to its own command** to keep the standard loop body lean
(ADR-006 of PLAN-latency-worktree-step-preview) — the standard iter body below
does NOT apply to these goals. Instead:

- **Claude Code:** read and follow `.claude/commands/hm/loop-p5-batch.md`.
- **Codex:** invoke the `hm-loop-p5-batch` skill.

That asset owns the full per-batch procedure, `p5-batch-all` handling, the
convergence predicate, and the worktree contract. This path is NOT routed
through `autoloop_driver.run()` (ADR-013 R2 requires the slash command to
handle batching).

